{"id":"epigallocatechin-gallate","cid":65064,"subject":"self","props":{"cid":65064,"title":"Epigallocatechin Gallate","formula":"C22H18O11","mw":458.4,"exactMass":458.08491139,"iupac":"[(2R,3R)-5,7-dihydroxy-2-(3,4,5-trihydroxyphenyl)-3,4-dihydro-2H-chromen-3-yl] 3,4,5-trihydroxybenzoate","smiles":"C1[C@H]([C@H](OC2=CC(=CC(=C21)O)O)C3=CC(=C(C(=C3)O)O)O)OC(=O)C4=CC(=C(C(=C4)O)O)O","inchi":"InChI=1S/C22H18O11/c23-10-5-12(24)11-7-18(33-22(31)9-3-15(27)20(30)16(28)4-9)21(32-17(11)6-10)8-1-13(25)19(29)14(26)2-8/h1-6,18,21,23-30H,7H2/t18-,21-/m1/s1","inchikey":"WMBWREPUVVBILR-WIYYLYMNSA-N","xlogp":1.2,"tpsa":197,"complexity":667,"charge":0,"hbd":8,"hba":11,"rotb":4,"heavy":33,"stereo":2,"units":1},"cas":"989-51-5","synonyms":["(-)-Epigallocatechin gallate","EGCG","Epigallocatechin gallate","Epigallocatechin-3-gallate","Tea catechin","(-)-Epigallocatechin-3-o-gallate","Teavigo","(-)-Epigallocatechol gallate","L-Epigallocatechin gallate","PF-EGCg 90","NVP-XAA 723","epigallocatechin-3-O-gallate"],"descriptions":[{"text":"(-)-epigallocatechin 3-gallate is a gallate ester obtained by the formal condensation of gallic acid with the (3R)-hydroxy group of ()-epigallocatechin. It has a role as a geroprotector, an antioxidant, an antineoplastic agent, a neuroprotective agent, a Hsp90 inhibitor, an apoptosis inducer and a plant metabolite. It is a polyphenol, a gallate ester and a member of flavans. It is functionally related to a (-)-epigallocatechin.","source":"ChEBI","url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:4806"}],"experimental":[{"key":"Physical Description","values":["Solid"],"source":"Human Metabolome Database (HMDB)"},{"key":"Melting Point","values":["140 - 142 °C"],"source":"Human Metabolome Database (HMDB)"},{"key":"LogP","values":["1.08"],"source":"SangsterLogP"}],"ghs":{"signal":"Warning","pictograms":[{"code":"GHS07","label":"Irritant"},{"code":"GHS09","label":"Environmental Hazard"}],"hazards":["H302 (72.7%): Harmful if swallowed","H317 (72.7%): May